This is the source code for Dave Stampe's polyblit routines as used in
the REND386 package.  They are written in 386 assembly language; if you're
not familiar with it, please don't ask Dave a lot of questions -- your
local library should have a book 386 assembly language programming.

In fact, if you're not familiar with assembler, you shouldn't really
need this source for anything; just use polyblit.lib instead.

Please be aware that all of Dave Stampe's code is copyrighted; you may
use it for non-commercial purposes, but if you want to use it in a product
you intend to sell (including shareware) please contact Dave at the e-mail
